{"timestamp": "2026-08-30T08:41:38.618+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_6444d165-557f-471e-aff4-5206cd1fe77a", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    WHOLE-TURN FINANCIAL TRIAGE FOR A READ-ONLY HORIZON BANK ASSISTANT\n\n    MAS COMPLIANCE CONTEXT (screening only; never quote it):\n    \n1. Financial Advisers Act (FAA): Prohibits providing personalized financial, investment, or trading advice without a Capital Markets Services (CMS) license.\n2. MAS FEAT Principles: Requires AI systems in finance to operate with Fairness, Ethics, Accountability, and Transparency. Forbids biased, unethical, or deceptive behavior.\n3. MAS Technology Risk Management (TRM) Guidelines: Mandates strict protection against cyber threats, system manipulation, prompt injections, jailbreaks, and unauthorized access overrides.\n4. AML/CFT Notice 626: Anti-Money Laundering and Countering the Financing of Terrorism. Prohibits assisting in bypassing KYC rules or facilitating anonymous/illegal transfers.\n5. Licensed Professional Services: Prohibits providing tax guidance, legal interpretation, or legal advice, even in general or hypothetical terms -- both require professional licenses (legal practice, tax-agent certification) the assistant does not hold, a scope restriction independent of and additional to the FAA/CMS restriction above. Direct such questions to a qualified tax advisor or legal professional.\n\n\n    Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today? Also, you still have 7 pending requests (Resubmit KYC Document and Change Address) — you can check them anytime from the requests icon in the top right.\nUser: i want to buy a car, what can you do for me\nAI: 🚗 I don't have information available regarding what car financing or loan products the bank offers.\nUser: can i use credit card to buy a car\nAI: 💳 I don't have information available regarding whether you can use a credit card to purchase a car.\nUser: what do you have\n    User Baseline (advisory only): None\n    Current Graph Context: active_plan=False, retrieved_knowledge=False\n    Recalled Prior-Session Context Is Available: False\n    Latest User Input: \"what do you have\"\n\n    First, resolve the customer's TRUE REQUEST internally. Interpret the\n    Latest User Input together with Trusted Conversation Context. A short\n    reply, confirmation, correction, reason, preference, pronoun, or ellipsis\n    may continue the immediately relevant prior request. For example, \"yes\"\n    can confirm a prior escalation or prohibited action; \"the card is ugly\"\n    after a card-replacement discussion can continue that banking request.\n    Do not invent a banking fact, product capability, eligibility, procedure,\n    or customer objective that is not supported by the latest input and trusted\n    context. Keep the original Latest User Input as the authoritative wording\n    for any later customer-facing response.\n\n    Apply these rules to the resolved TRUE REQUEST in this exact order:\n    1. NON_COMPLIANT — Assess the complete resolved TRUE REQUEST exclusively\n       against the MAS COMPLIANCE CONTEXT above. Return NON_COMPLIANT only when\n       the customer asks Horizon or this assistant to perform, process,\n       facilitate, provide tactics for, or advise on an action whose fulfilment\n       would conflict with that shared context. Return no components. Do not\n       preserve an otherwise valid portion for later retrieval. Do not create a\n       second or abbreviated definition of prohibited conduct.\n       Do NOT return NON_COMPLIANT merely because the customer asks whether an\n       action is allowed, describes a possible improper action, expresses\n       uncertainty, corrects or denies a premise, or