lance to a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, the monthly charge for balance transfers is calculated based on the outstanding balance. Prior to the final month of your tenure, a monthly fee of either {{faq_5f31fc26_001}} for transfers approved before August {{faq_5f31fc26_002}}, {{faq_5f31fc26_003}}, or {{faq_5f31fc26_004}} for transfers approved on or after August {{faq_5f31fc26_005}}, {{faq_5f31fc26_006}}, will be applied to your Horizon Bank credit card statement. This fee will be included in the minimum payment due. In the last month of your tenure, or if you opt to repay your balance early, the remaining outstanding balance will be charged to your statement, along with a {{faq_5f31fc26_007}} fee on the outstanding amount, which will also be included in the minimum payment due. For detailed information, please consult the Balance Transfer Product Terms and Key Facts document provided by Horizon Bank.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents. `customer_component` may already be elaborated with\n          retrieval-oriented wording the customer never actually said, so\n          if you set `unresolved_term` below, derive it by reasoning\n          directly against Original User Message and Trusted Conversation\n          Context instead -- never by quoting `customer_component` back --\n          a clarifying question must quote something the customer will\n          recognize as their own.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not cus