{"timestamp": "2026-08-31T09:04:30.115+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_85f49f45-2189-476c-b0d0-93b44d06504b", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): i want to buy a car\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today? Also, you still have 3 pending Resubmit KYC Document requests — you can check them anytime from the requests icon in the top right.\n\nWould you like to continue discussing car loan financing options?\nUser: i want to buy a house\nAI: Sorry, for your request, I can't provide an answer — it's not a product or service Horizon currently offers.\nUser: i want to buy a car\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"mapping_reason\": \"The customer is inquiring about financing for a car, which maps to the Personal_Loan product family and the General Inquiries intent.\", \"procedural\": \"Submit your application through our online portal or visit a branch with your income documents.\", \"policy\": \"Loan approval is subject to credit assessment, income verification, and meeting our minimum age requirements.\", \"conceptual\": \"A car loan is a fixed-term financing product designed to help individuals purchase a new or used vehicle.\", \"target_commercial_product\": [\"Personal_Loan\", \"Horizon_APP\"], \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Loan And Credit Management\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\"], \"alternate_product_reason\": \"Financing options for vehicles can sometimes be managed or tracked through the Horizon_APP interface.\", \"alternate_products\": [\"Horizon_APP\"], \"search_territory\": \"in_scope\", \"customer_component\": \"I would like to inquire about car loan financing options.\", \"direct_query\": \"I would like to inquire about car loan financing options.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit your application through our online portal or visit a branch with your income documents.\", \"policy\": \"Loan approval is subject to credit assessment, income verification, and meeting our minimum age requirements.\", \"conceptual\": \"A car loan is a fixed-term financing product designed to help individuals purchase a new or used vehicle.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The supplied parents discuss credit card balance transfers, which is a distinct product from the car loan financing requested by the customer. The parents do not provide any information regarding car loan applications, eligibility, or the financing process.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_75ed6e4d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical timeframe for my loan to be approved?\\n\\nAnswer: - The vast majority of loans are approved and the amount is deposited into your Horizon savings account in about {{faq_75ed6e4d_001}} seconds.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_f9cce3c1\", \"content\": \"Question: If my Instant Loan request is declined, can I still submit applications for other Horizon Bank products such as a credit card or a savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - Absolutely. A declined loan does not prevent you from applying for other Horizon Bank offerings. You simply need to start a new application tailored to the specific product you wish to obtain.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1946c44f\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps should I follow to request an Instant Loan from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - Open the Horizon App, go to the **Money** menu, and select **Loan** to initiate the process.\\n- If you are not yet a Horizon customer, first download the Horizon App, then navigate to **Product Selection** and choose **Instant Loan** to begin your application.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_0ae0bb51\", \"content\": \"Question: Do I qualify for Horizon Bank’s Instant Loan offering?\\n\\nAnswer: - **For current Horizon Bank clients:**\\n  * You need to possess a Horizon credit card and have adequate unused credit limit.\\n- **For new applicants:**\\n  * Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply for the Instant Loan.\\n  * Every submission will be subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment.\\n\\nYou may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria:\\n- You are aged between {{faq_0ae0bb51_001}} and {{faq_0ae0bb51_002}} years.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_003}} if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_004}} if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_1_scope\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1_scope\", \"mapping_reason\": \"Since the user wants to buy a car, they may need to manage their existing savings or liquidity to fund the purchase, which relates to Deposit_Account and the Payments And Transfers intent.\", \"procedural\": \"Initiate a transfer from your savings account to your external bank account for vehicle payment.\", \"policy\": \"Daily transfer limits apply to all outgoing transactions from your deposit account for security purposes.\", \"conceptual\": \"A deposit account provides the necessary liquidity and transaction capabilities for making large personal purchases.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"Payments And Transfers\"], \"search_territory\": \"adjacent_scope\", \"source_task_id\": \"task_1\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"customer_component\": \"I would like to inquire about car loan financing options.\", \"direct_query\": \"I would like to inquire about car loan financing options.\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Initiate a transfer from your savings account to your external bank account for vehicle payment.\", \"policy\": \"Daily transfer limits apply to all outgoing transactions from your deposit account for security purposes.\", \"conceptual\": \"A deposit account provides the necessary liquidity and transaction capabilities for making large personal purchases.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_730ac28e\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank safeguard its customers' electronic payment transactions, and what responsibilities do account holders have in protecting their accounts?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we adhere to the E-Payments User Protection Guidelines set forth by the Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS), which outline the roles of both financial institutions and consumers in preventing and addressing unauthorized and erroneous transactions. To ensure the security of your protected account, which includes any account with a balance exceeding {{faq_730ac28e_001}} or equivalent, capable of electronic transactions, and issued by a relevant payment service provider, please follow these best practices: \\n   - Only download the Horizon App from authorized sources and regularly update your browser and operating system.\\n   - Provide accurate contact information and opt-in to receive transaction notifications to stay informed about your account activity.\\n   - Safeguard your One-Time Passwords (OTPs) sent via the Horizon App or SMS, and secure access to your protected account.\\n   - Carefully review risk warning messages and content from Horizon Bank before proceeding with payment transactions or engaging in high-risk activities.\\n   - Verify website addresses and phone numbers through official channels to avoid potential scams.\\n   - Understand the risks associated with high-risk activities and take necessary precautions.\\n   - Promptly report any suspicious or unauthorized activity on your account, and utilize the self-service 'kill switch' feature provided by Horizon Bank to block further access.\\n   - Cooperate with Horizon Bank by providing detailed information about unauthorized transactions and filing a police report if you suspect you've been a victim of fraud or scam.\\n   For comprehensive details on the E-Payment Guidelines, please visit the MAS website at https://www.mas.gov.sg/regulation/guidelines/e-payments-user-protection-guidelines.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7d49c937\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the available ways to fund my Horizon Bank savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Method {{faq_7d49c937_001}} – Bank transfer via FAST**\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_002}}. Log in to the online portal of your other bank.\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_003}}. Add your Horizon Bank savings account as a local beneficiary, providing the beneficiary name and your Horizon savings account number.\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_004}}. Initiate the FAST transfer; the money will be credited to your Horizon account shortly.\\n- **Method {{faq_7d49c937_005}} – PayNow**\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_006}}. If your mobile number or NRIC/FIN is already linked to PayNow with a different bank, first remove that linkage.\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_007}}. Open the Horizon App, tap the Payments tab, and select “Register for PayNow” if you haven’t done so already.\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_008}}. Complete the registration, then send a PayNow payment to the registered mobile number or NRIC/FIN; the funds will appear in your Horizon savings account.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_13757d59\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to arrange for periodic deposits into my Horizon Bank savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: Indeed, you can establish a recurring local funds transfer, such as a Standing Instruction or Scheduled Transfer, from other banks to your specified Horizon Bank savings account. To do so, simply utilize the banking channels provided by other banks to specify the desired payment frequency, amount, and the Horizon Bank account number where you wish to receive the funds.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_beeeec2d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for paying my Horizon credit card statement using money from my Horizon savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - Open the Horizon App and sign in.\\n- Navigate to the \\\"Credit Card\\\" section and choose \\\"Pay Card.\\\"\\n- Your Horizon Savings Account will appear as a payment source; select it and follow the prompts to complete the transaction.\\n- To ensure timely payments, you can also enable AutoPay, which will automatically draw the required amount from your savings account each billing cycle.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents. `customer_component` may already be elaborated with\n          retrieval-oriented wording the customer never actually said, so\n          if you set `unresolved_term` below, derive it by reasoning\n          directly against Original User Message and Trusted Conversation\n          Context instead -- never by quoting `customer_component` back --\n          a clarifying question must quote something the customer will\n          recognize as their own.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - TERRITORY CEILING (Extra Effort v2.0): when `task.search_territory`\n          is `\"adjacent_scope\"`, this task is a deliberate scope-expansion\n          companion -- by construction, its own product/intent is DIFFERENT\n          from what the customer literally asked about, offered only as\n          related information that might still help. Its status may never\n          be SUFFICIENT, no matter how well its parents match it -- cap at\n          PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when they contain a genuinely useful related\n          fact, INSUFFICIENT when they don't. A normal task\n          (`search_territory` absent or `\"in_scope\"`) has no such ceiling.\n          Never set `likely_ambiguous_request`/`unresolved_term` for an\n          `\"adjacent_scope\"` task either -- clarification-authoring for\n          this subquery belongs exclusively to its `\"in_scope\"` sibling\n          task, which reviews the same underlying request.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains