{"timestamp": "2026-08-31T13:32:35.122+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_cdc9d5a8-6c24-4d48-b30d-ac9a21846ab7", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): I am asking about using my savings account for buying a house.\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today? Also, you still have 3 pending Resubmit KYC Document requests — you can check them anytime from the requests icon in the top right.\n\nWould you like to continue discussing your options for funding your car purchase with a personal loan or your savings?\nUser: can i buy a house\nAI: To help you with buying a house, are you asking about a personal loan or using your savings account? 🏡\nUser: I am asking about a personal loan to help with buying a house.\nAI: Loan Eligibility Criteria: For current Horizon Bank clients, you need to possess a Horizon credit card and have an adequate unused credit limit. For new applicants, Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply, and every submission is subject to Horizon Bank's credit-worthiness assessment. You may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria: you are aged between 21 and 65 years; your annual income is at least S$30,000 if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident; or your annual income is at least S$60,000 if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\nApproval and Deposit Timeframe: The vast majority of loans are approved and the amount is deposited into your Horizon savings account in about 60 seconds.\nUser: I am asking about using my savings account for buying a house.\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"mapping_reason\": \"The customer is inquiring about the usage of their 'savings account' (Deposit_Account) for a specific financial goal (buying a house). 'General Inquiries' is the appropriate intent for understanding how a savings account can be utilized for such purposes.\", \"procedural\": \"Access your savings account balance and transaction history through the Horizon mobile app or online banking portal.\", \"policy\": \"Savings accounts are subject to minimum balance requirements and applicable interest rate structures as defined by account terms.\", \"conceptual\": \"A savings account is a deposit account designed for holding funds securely while earning interest over time.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"General Inquiries\"], \"alternate_product_reason\": \"If the inquiry relates to the digital management of the account for this goal, the Horizon_APP is a plausible functional alternative.\", \"alternate_products\": [\"Horizon_APP\"], \"search_territory\": \"in_scope\", \"customer_component\": \"I am asking about using my savings account for buying a house.\", \"direct_query\": \"I am asking about using my savings account for buying a house.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Access your savings account balance and transaction history through the Horizon mobile app or online banking portal.\", \"policy\": \"Savings accounts are subject to minimum balance requirements and applicable interest rate structures as defined by account terms.\", \"conceptual\": \"A savings account is a deposit account designed for holding funds securely while earning interest over time.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_93d37190\", \"content\": \"Question: After opening a savings account, am I eligible to apply for a Horizon credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: - Eligibility criteria:\\n  - You are between {{faq_93d37190_001}} and {{faq_93d37190_002}} years old and earn at least {{faq_93d37190_003}} annually, and you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n  - You are older than {{faq_93d37190_004}} years and earn at least {{faq_93d37190_005}} annually, and you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\nOnly Singapore citizens and permanent residents can hold both a Horizon savings account and a Horizon credit card. To submit an application, go to **More > More for you** within the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_13757d59\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to arrange for periodic deposits into my Horizon Bank savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: Indeed, you can establish a recurring local funds transfer, such as a Standing Instruction or Scheduled Transfer, from other banks to your specified Horizon Bank savings account. To do so, simply utilize the banking channels provided by other banks to specify the desired payment frequency, amount, and the Horizon Bank account number where you wish to receive the funds.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_daff2a37\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the turnaround time for paying a credit‑card bill using funds from my Horizon savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - The payment is posted instantly to the designated credit card, and you will receive an immediate confirmation.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_10f9fec0\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements to open a new Horizon Bank account?\\n\\nAnswer: To initiate the application process for a Horizon Bank account, simply utilize your mobile device and authenticate through MyInfo, which will expedite the pre-filling of your application in a secure manner. For non-Singaporean residents, please be prepared to upload a valid passport and relevant income documentation, particularly if you are applying for a Horizon credit card.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents. `customer_component` may already be elaborated with\n          retrieval-oriented wording the customer never actually said, so\n          if you set `unresolved_term` below, derive it by reasoning\n          directly against Original User Message and Trusted Conversation\n          Context instead -- never by quoting `customer_component` back --\n          a clarifying question must quote something the customer will\n          recognize as their own.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - TERRITORY CEILING (Extra Effort v2.0): when `task.search_territory`\n          is `\"adjacent_scope\"`, this task is a deliberate scope-expansion\n          companion -- by construction, its own product/intent is DIFFERENT\n          from what the customer literally asked about, offered only as\n          related information that might still help. Its status may never\n          be SUFFICIENT, no matter how well its parents match it -- cap at\n          PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when they contain a genuinely useful related\n          fact, INSUFFICIENT when they don't. A normal task\n          (`search_territory` absent or `\"in_scope\"`) has no such ceiling.\n          Never set `likely_ambiguous_request`/`unresolved_term` for an\n          `\"adjacent_scope\"` task either -- clarification-authoring for\n          this subquery belongs exclusively to its `\"in_scope\"` sibling\n          task, which reviews the same underlying request.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as